WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:04.921
It seems today that all you see

00:04.922 --> 00:08.174
Is violence in movies and sex on TV

00:08.175 --> 00:11.928
But where are those
good old-fashioned values

00:11.929 --> 00:15.056
On which we used to rely?

00:15.057 --> 00:18.309
Lucky there's a family guy

00:18.310 --> 00:21.604
Lucky there's a man
who positively can do

00:21.605 --> 00:23.189
All the things that make us

00:23.190 --> 00:25.024
Laugh and cry

00:25.025 --> 00:30.155
He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy!

00:38.789 --> 00:40.581
Go, Stewie!

00:40.582 --> 00:42.416
Ha! Isn't this exciting?

00:42.417 --> 00:44.502
Yeah, but I don't like
little Kyle Kaepernick

00:44.503 --> 00:46.254
kneeling during the national anthem.

00:48.590 --> 00:51.092
Boo! Get on your feet!

00:51.093 --> 00:53.261
Boo! Down in front.

00:53.262 --> 00:55.806
Okay, need to stay focused.

00:56.974 --> 00:58.266
What are those for?

00:58.267 --> 01:00.268
Power songs that get me focused.

01:00.269 --> 01:03.646
The wheels on the bus go round and round

01:03.647 --> 01:06.148
All through the town.

01:06.149 --> 01:08.985
It's the same thing Ryan Lochte
listens to before a race.

01:08.986 --> 01:11.112
Stewie, you're taking this
way too seriously.

01:11.113 --> 01:13.990
It's a meaningless event,
like a bar mitzvah.

01:13.991 --> 01:15.533
Today you are a man.

01:15.534 --> 01:17.493
- Great. Can I drive?
- No.

01:17.494 --> 01:18.786
- Can I vote?
- No.

01:18.787 --> 01:19.954
- Can I drink?
- No.

01:19.955 --> 01:21.163
- Can I have sex?
- No.

01:21.164 --> 01:23.333
- Can I cash the checks?
- Yes!

01:38.181 --> 01:40.349
Lois, why'd we got to come here?

01:40.350 --> 01:42.184
This place is a bunch of rich snobs.

01:42.185 --> 01:44.645
We have lunch with my parents
twice a year.

01:44.646 --> 01:45.813
Consider yourself lucky.

01:45.814 --> 01:47.356
Under normal circumstances,

01:47.357 --> 01:49.400
you'd never be allowed
in a place like this.

01:49.401 --> 01:51.152
Griffin, come on.
They're waiting for your order.

01:51.153 --> 01:53.529
Sorry. Do you have oysters?

01:53.530 --> 01:55.823
- We do not.
- Aw, shucks.

01:59.369 --> 02:01.370
Damn it, Griffin,
you've been staring at that menu

02:01.371 --> 02:04.233
for five minutes,
and you peed your pants.

02:04.234 --> 02:06.375
Um, do you have oysters?

02:06.376 --> 02:08.629
Get up. They have to clean the chair.

02:13.216 --> 02:16.677
Hey, Brian, you don't have
a metal detector on you, do you?

02:16.678 --> 02:18.929
Okay, Stewie, you got a medal.
Way to go.

02:18.930 --> 02:20.765
Do I sense a hint of jealousy?

02:20.766 --> 02:22.391
Stewie, didn't it strike you as odd

02:22.392 --> 02:24.185
that everyone got a medal?

02:24.186 --> 02:26.687
You didn't win anything.
It's a participant medal.

02:26.688 --> 02:28.522
They give 'em to every kid with a pulse.

02:28.523 --> 02:30.858
And like every other medal
or award you've ever gotten,

02:30.859 --> 02:32.485
it means nothing.

02:32.486 --> 02:34.237
What?

02:39.368 --> 02:41.410
Stewie, I-I'm sorry.

02:41.411 --> 02:44.372
I-I shouldn't have said that.
I lost my temper.

02:44.373 --> 02:47.542
Slow down!

02:58.595 --> 03:00.638
No, no, no, no, no.

03:00.639 --> 03:02.139
How could I be such a fool?

03:02.140 --> 03:04.434
This is a wall of lies.

03:05.644 --> 03:07.103
And that's a hole of lies.

03:07.104 --> 03:09.564
Everything I've ever won is worthless!

03:12.442 --> 03:13.777
Aah!

03:15.654 --> 03:18.115
You won't make a fool of me any longer.

03:22.119 --> 03:24.328
Oh, no! It's all right, Stewie.

03:24.329 --> 03:27.373
Stay calm. This is why
we have a house fire captain.

03:27.374 --> 03:30.584
Okay, when I read your name,
please respond with a "here."

03:30.585 --> 03:32.962
- Griffin, Mac.
- It's Meg.

03:32.963 --> 03:34.255
Sorry, it looks like "Mac."

03:34.256 --> 03:36.966
- Griffin, Liam.
- It's Lois.

03:36.967 --> 03:39.678
Again, please respond with "here."

03:43.348 --> 03:46.767
Oh, my God, Chris is still in there!

03:46.768 --> 03:48.519
Somebody save Chris!

03:59.030 --> 04:01.950
You know what? He's earned that.

04:13.211 --> 04:15.296
God, look at this place.

04:15.297 --> 04:17.523
Our whole house is destroyed.

04:17.524 --> 04:19.198
Oh, here comes the insurance guy.

04:19.199 --> 04:21.677
Everyone start crying about
losing your new golf clubs

04:21.678 --> 04:23.596
and Grant Wood's American Gothic.

04:23.597 --> 04:25.055
Oh...

04:25.056 --> 04:28.851
my new golf clubs
with the titanium shafts.

04:28.852 --> 04:32.480
Oh, my classic depiction
of the austere steadfastness

04:32.481 --> 04:34.064
of rural America!

04:34.065 --> 04:36.192
You know, I don't care.
It's not my money.

04:36.193 --> 04:37.693
Oh.

04:37.694 --> 04:39.361
Peter, I spoke with my parents,

04:39.362 --> 04:41.697
and we can live with them
until our house is fixed.

04:41.698 --> 04:44.200
Great. It's gonna suck worse
than Mueslix.

04:44.201 --> 04:46.410
You know, the German health cereal?

04:46.411 --> 04:48.245
Guten Morgen. Try me.

04:48.246 --> 04:50.414
I am made of oats and fiber.

04:50.415 --> 04:51.874
Okay. Sounds healthy.

04:51.875 --> 04:53.584
Ja. Also, I am German

04:53.585 --> 04:55.419
and wouldn't mind watching you crap.

04:55.420 --> 04:57.505
- Uh, I don't know.
- Come, come.

04:57.506 --> 04:59.757
It will be mine and yours little secret.

04:59.758 --> 05:02.510
Just the two of us.
Please, take me home.

05:02.511 --> 05:04.637
Uh, okay. But just you.

05:04.638 --> 05:07.097
I don't feel safe now.

05:07.098 --> 05:09.558
Stop talking!
Concentrate on the pooping!

05:09.559 --> 05:12.102
Mueslix, the weird European cereal

05:12.103 --> 05:14.231
that likes to watch you poop.

05:20.821 --> 05:23.614
Aw, why we got to stay
with your parents?

05:23.615 --> 05:25.115
You know, sometimes I get the feeling

05:25.116 --> 05:26.368
they don't respect me.

05:56.690 --> 05:58.941
Thank you for not interrupting my bit.

05:58.942 --> 06:00.443
Come on in.

06:02.070 --> 06:04.071
Wow, check out this media room.

06:04.072 --> 06:06.115
Maybe you burning down the house
wasn't so bad.

06:06.116 --> 06:07.950
My actions were justified.

06:07.951 --> 06:09.910
I'd been fed a massive societal lie

06:09.911 --> 06:13.081
in the form of participant awards.

06:15.500 --> 06:19.295
Hey, kids, how would you like
to hear this on the screen

06:19.296 --> 06:21.839
instead of the great show
you came to see?

06:24.301 --> 06:27.094
That's what you sound like. Honest.

06:27.095 --> 06:29.096
Please cooperate and do your part

06:29.097 --> 06:31.515
in keeping this theater quiet,
so everyone,

06:31.516 --> 06:33.934
including you, can enjoy it.

06:33.935 --> 06:36.353
Remember, lots of adults and kids, too,

06:36.354 --> 06:38.314
paid admission to enjoy the show.

06:38.315 --> 06:42.568
We must insist on absolute quiet.

06:42.569 --> 06:44.987
Otherwise, we will be forced to evict

06:44.988 --> 06:47.364
all disturbance makers from the theater.

06:47.365 --> 06:51.368
Those asked to leave today
will be refused admission

06:51.369 --> 06:52.995
to this theater in the future.

06:52.996 --> 06:54.622
Thank you.

06:54.623 --> 06:56.373
Wow, what a dick.

06:56.374 --> 06:57.791
Good evening, I'm Tom Tucker.

06:57.792 --> 06:59.501
I've deleted all my old tweets,

06:59.502 --> 07:01.670
so don't even bother looking
for bad stuff.

07:01.671 --> 07:03.380
Screen grabs can be faked.

07:03.381 --> 07:05.341
But, first, it's that time of year again

07:05.342 --> 07:07.384
for the annual Quahog Pie Cook-off.

07:07.385 --> 07:11.138
The winner will take home
the coveted Pie Champ trophy.

07:11.139 --> 07:13.349
Brian, this could be
my chance to finally win

07:13.350 --> 07:14.850
a legitimate award.

07:14.851 --> 07:16.393
- You think you're up to it?
- Of course.

07:16.394 --> 07:17.978
I just have to apply myself.

07:17.979 --> 07:20.022
Like Chris, when he worked
at that casino.

07:20.023 --> 07:21.899
No more bets. The money that
could have gone to your kids

07:21.900 --> 07:23.859
is gone. No more bets.

07:23.860 --> 07:25.736
The money you worked hard for is gone.

07:25.737 --> 07:28.530
Fools, fools, fools.

07:28.531 --> 07:31.533
Ooh, double zero.
Nobody thinks about that one.

07:31.534 --> 07:33.953
And guy walks quickly away
from table without a word,

07:33.954 --> 07:36.413
replaced by an older white man
with a much younger black woman.

07:36.414 --> 07:38.625
No more bets. No more bets.

07:41.628 --> 07:45.214
Brian, are you ready
for my grand creation?

07:45.215 --> 07:47.591
- Serve it up, bitch.
- Well, that was uncalled for.

07:47.592 --> 07:50.178
But get ready to be wowed.

07:52.514 --> 07:54.598
What the... This is mud.

07:54.599 --> 07:56.058
Yes. It's a mud pie.

07:56.059 --> 07:57.935
I used Legos for the fruit.

07:57.936 --> 08:00.020
Stewie, you can't submit this.
It's inedible.

08:00.021 --> 08:01.730
Okay, now I know you're full of crap,

08:01.731 --> 08:04.066
because everyone else loves it.

08:04.067 --> 08:07.069
Mmm, num-num-num-num-nah.

08:07.070 --> 08:09.238
So delicious, Stewie.

08:09.239 --> 08:11.074
Best pie ever.

08:12.701 --> 08:15.661
Wow! Tastes great, Stewie.

08:15.662 --> 08:18.706
Mmm, so good.

08:18.707 --> 08:20.124
Boy, oh, boy, oh, boy.

08:20.125 --> 08:22.418
Not so hammy, Meg. He's not an idiot.

08:22.419 --> 08:24.086
Stewie, can't you see they're faking it

08:24.087 --> 08:25.129
to make you feel good?

08:25.130 --> 08:26.381
What are you talking about?

08:27.215 --> 08:29.341
Wow!

08:29.342 --> 08:33.387
Mmm. Num-num-num-num-nah.

08:33.388 --> 08:36.890
So good.

08:36.891 --> 08:40.978
We must insist on absolute quiet.

08:40.979 --> 08:43.480
My God, you're right.

08:43.481 --> 08:46.400
They're all just lying
to protect my feelings.

08:46.401 --> 08:48.318
This pie is garbage!

08:48.319 --> 08:50.612
And the contest is next week.
I have to drop out.

08:50.613 --> 08:52.740
No, you don't.
You just got to do the work.

08:52.741 --> 08:54.408
Stewie, you're a smart kid.

08:54.409 --> 08:57.161
I know you can bake a pie,
and I'll help you.

08:57.162 --> 08:59.288
You will? Thank you, Brian.

08:59.289 --> 09:01.957
This calls for champagne.

09:01.958 --> 09:03.834
Pop.

09:03.835 --> 09:06.336
Glug, glug, glug.

09:06.337 --> 09:08.172
Bottoms up.

09:08.173 --> 09:10.299
Go with it.

09:10.300 --> 09:11.800
Ugh. Korbel?

09:11.801 --> 09:13.469
- It's not Korbel. It's...
- Go with it.

09:13.470 --> 09:15.971
Yes, I had some left over
from Denise's wedding.

09:15.972 --> 09:17.848
- Who's Denise?
- Go with it.

09:17.849 --> 09:20.476
Fine. How is Denise?
Did she have the abortion?

09:20.477 --> 09:22.186
- Abortion?
- Go with it.

09:22.187 --> 09:24.980
No, her alarm didn't go off,
so she missed it.

09:24.981 --> 09:26.982
So, Brian, is this your first orgy?

09:26.983 --> 09:28.401
Not going with it.

09:34.032 --> 09:36.492
Peter, would you like to join us
in a parlor game?

09:36.493 --> 09:38.118
Parlor game?

09:38.119 --> 09:39.661
Lois, why do you always
start talking like a snob

09:39.662 --> 09:41.121
when you're around your parents?

09:41.122 --> 09:43.165
What? It's the way I was brought up.

09:43.166 --> 09:45.209
I know, let's play "The Minister's Cat."

09:45.210 --> 09:46.710
I don't know what that is.

09:46.711 --> 09:49.214
It's simple. In alphabetical order. Go.

09:51.174 --> 09:53.176
The minister's cat is an affable cat.

09:54.844 --> 09:56.845
The minister's cat is a boisterous cat.

09:56.846 --> 09:58.347
Penrose!

09:58.348 --> 10:00.350
The minister's cat is a covetous cat.

10:01.267 --> 10:04.520
The minister's cat is a devious cat.

10:04.521 --> 10:06.563
The minister's cat's an eclectic cat.

10:06.564 --> 10:07.856
Peter, your turn. Go.

10:07.857 --> 10:09.358
- Wh-What?
- Peter, hurry.

10:09.359 --> 10:10.984
I don't... I don't know this cat.

10:10.985 --> 10:13.028
Damn it, Peter, you ruined the game!

10:13.029 --> 10:16.198
Peter, perhaps the word
you were looking for is...

10:16.199 --> 10:17.866
"forgotten."

10:17.867 --> 10:20.744
Midnight

10:20.745 --> 10:25.707
Not a sound from the pavement

10:25.708 --> 10:30.712
Has the moon lost her memory?

10:30.713 --> 10:35.217
She is smiling alone.

10:35.218 --> 10:37.219
You kids are too young to remember that,

10:37.220 --> 10:40.055
but your parents are gonna hate it.

10:44.269 --> 10:46.771
Finally, a place to escape.

10:51.609 --> 10:53.110
Oh, hey, Babs.

10:53.111 --> 10:55.612
Hello, Peter. What brings you out here?

10:55.613 --> 10:57.906
I had to get away from that stupid game.

10:57.907 --> 11:01.285
I don't know, whenever I'm here,
I feel out of place.

11:01.286 --> 11:04.372
It's just a different world
than I'm used to.

11:09.919 --> 11:11.920
Bring that up again,
and we'll vote on it.

11:11.921 --> 11:14.256
Whoa, where'd you learn
a line like that?

11:14.257 --> 11:16.925
Oh, there's a lot
you don't know about me.

11:16.926 --> 11:19.928
You know, Peter,
you and I are not so different.

11:19.929 --> 11:21.805
You struggle to get erections, too?

11:21.806 --> 11:25.642
You may think I've always been a
part of this high-society world,

11:25.643 --> 11:28.812
but I wasn't born
with a silver spoon in my mouth.

11:28.813 --> 11:31.190
Well, that probably would've
torn your mom's uterus.

11:31.191 --> 11:34.443
My point is, I'm not from
an upper-crust world, either.

11:34.444 --> 11:37.112
I just had to act that way
to impress Carter,

11:37.113 --> 11:38.780
who cared about that stuff.

11:38.781 --> 11:41.116
I was struggling
to be something I wasn't.

11:41.117 --> 11:43.368
In many ways, I still am.

11:43.369 --> 11:44.953
There's an Ed Sheeran song

11:44.954 --> 11:47.080
for every emotion
you're feeling right now.

11:47.081 --> 11:48.832
Ooh, no, thank you.

11:48.833 --> 11:50.584
You know, I like hanging out with you.

11:50.585 --> 11:52.252
Hey, what do you say
we ditch this stuffy place

11:52.253 --> 11:54.755
- and head to the Clam?
- The Drunken Clam?

11:54.756 --> 11:57.174
Why, I haven't been there in decades.

11:57.175 --> 11:58.800
I'd love to.

11:58.801 --> 12:00.636
To the Babsmobile!

12:03.598 --> 12:05.974
You got vehicles
with your face on 'em, too?

12:05.975 --> 12:07.643
You know it, stinky.

12:07.644 --> 12:10.563
Oh, I didn't like being called stinky.

12:18.821 --> 12:20.364
Babs, I got to hand it to you.

12:20.365 --> 12:22.658
You turned a crappy night
into something great.

12:22.659 --> 12:24.034
You know, I've never dropped
bowling balls

12:24.035 --> 12:26.662
from an overpass before.
They fall quick.

12:26.663 --> 12:29.665
That was the most fun
I've had in decades.

12:29.666 --> 12:33.085
It felt good to reconnect
with the girl I once was.

12:33.086 --> 12:35.212
Hey, listen, you got
to stay true to that girl.

12:35.213 --> 12:37.965
She's an amazing person. A real person.

12:37.966 --> 12:40.259
Not some stuffy Newport snob.

12:40.260 --> 12:43.303
Oh, sometimes I feel trapped
in this world,

12:43.304 --> 12:46.890
forever trying to live up
to everyone else's expectations,

12:46.891 --> 12:48.517
especially Carter's.

12:48.518 --> 12:50.894
Sounds like you've wasted
your entire life.

12:50.895 --> 12:52.729
Thank you, Peter.

12:52.730 --> 12:55.899
You've helped me
more than you know. Mwah.

12:55.900 --> 12:57.819
Yuck.

13:02.031 --> 13:03.865
Well, Brian, I've studied pie-making,

13:03.866 --> 13:06.743
and the key is to find the
absolute freshest ingredients.

13:06.744 --> 13:10.038
Therefore, we must go wherever
and whenever

13:10.039 --> 13:12.333
they're to be found.

13:18.756 --> 13:21.758
- Where are we?
- 1666, England.

13:21.759 --> 13:23.385
Home of Sir Isaac Newton

13:23.386 --> 13:25.888
and one of history's most famous apples.

13:28.224 --> 13:30.518
Which will be part of our pie.

13:33.229 --> 13:36.316
Gravity never happened!

13:40.069 --> 13:41.695
Good morning, family.

13:41.696 --> 13:44.239
And before anyone asks,
I brought this owl from home.

13:44.240 --> 13:46.742
I did not take it
from the enclosed owlery.

13:46.743 --> 13:49.494
Just want to make that clear.
Home-brought owl.

13:49.495 --> 13:52.122
Peter, what did the two of you
talk about last night?

13:52.123 --> 13:53.707
Yeah, who?

13:53.708 --> 13:56.043
You can see why I stole this
from the owlery...

13:56.044 --> 13:57.627
I-I mean brought it from home. Damn it!

13:57.628 --> 14:00.130
My mother. After your night together,

14:00.131 --> 14:01.923
she told Daddy she's leaving him.

14:01.924 --> 14:04.061
Yeah, who?

14:04.062 --> 14:05.552
All right, I'm already getting
tired of this owl.

14:05.553 --> 14:07.262
I'm gonna go put him back in the owlery.

14:07.263 --> 14:09.974
Peter, enough.
You've got to make this right.

14:13.519 --> 14:16.314
Now, that one seemed less earned.

14:32.205 --> 14:34.122
Babs, I've been looking
all over for you.

14:34.123 --> 14:37.125
- What are you doing here?
- This is my hometown, Peter.

14:37.126 --> 14:38.627
It's where I grew up.

14:38.628 --> 14:40.587
In fact, as a rebellious teen,

14:40.588 --> 14:42.672
I used to come down to this boardwalk

14:42.673 --> 14:46.510
and feed Alka-Seltzer tablets
to the seagulls.

14:48.221 --> 14:50.931
Babs, you got to come home.
Carter needs you.

14:50.932 --> 14:53.600
I'm sorry,
but I-I can't do that right now.

14:55.353 --> 14:58.522
Peter, you've been able
to stay true to who you were.

14:58.523 --> 15:00.816
I've lost touch with that.

15:00.817 --> 15:04.528
It's been buried
by Carter and his money.

15:04.529 --> 15:06.988
I want to find it again.

15:06.989 --> 15:09.825
Listen, Babs, I understand
what you're doing. I really do.

15:09.826 --> 15:11.868
Sometimes I feel suffocated by Lois

15:11.869 --> 15:14.538
and my stupid mother-in-law,
but you got to come home.

15:14.539 --> 15:17.457
I don't think so, Peter.

15:17.458 --> 15:19.209
You and Carter are meant for each other.

15:19.210 --> 15:20.710
You go together.

15:20.711 --> 15:23.004
L-Like the couple from the movie Grease.

15:23.005 --> 15:27.008
Mr. Rama-Lama-Lama-Ka-Dinga-
Da-Dinga-Dong, do you take

15:27.009 --> 15:29.886
Miss Shoo-Bop-Sha-Wadda-
Wadda-Yippity-Boom-De-Boom

15:29.887 --> 15:31.888
- to be your wife?
- I do.

15:31.889 --> 15:35.308
And Miss Shoo-Bop-Sha-Wadda-
Wadda-Yippity-Boom-De-Boom,

15:35.309 --> 15:39.479
do you take Mr. Rama-Lama-Lama-
Ka-Dinga-Da-Dinga-Dong

15:39.480 --> 15:41.815
- to be your husband?
- I do.

15:41.816 --> 15:43.483
If anyone objects to this union,

15:43.484 --> 15:46.069
speak now or forever hold your peace.

15:47.131 --> 15:49.992
Mr. Chang-Chang-Changity-Chang-Sha-Bop!

15:55.163 --> 15:57.038
Peter, where have you been?

15:57.039 --> 15:59.708
Listen, Carter, unless you want
to lose Babs forever,

15:59.709 --> 16:01.209
you better get down to Weekapaug.

16:01.210 --> 16:02.669
Why the hell would I do that?

16:02.670 --> 16:04.212
If you want to win her back,

16:04.213 --> 16:06.756
maybe, for once,
you try to fit into her world.

16:06.757 --> 16:08.842
You got to become a regular guy.

16:08.843 --> 16:11.011
What? No! Never!

16:11.012 --> 16:15.056
Daddy, Peter's right.
You got to do this for Mom.

16:15.057 --> 16:18.393
All right, fine. I'll take
a quick choke-myself-awake nap

16:18.394 --> 16:20.061
and be ready to go.

16:28.696 --> 16:31.532
All right. All right, let's go.

16:38.414 --> 16:41.249
- I'm so nervous.
- You made a damn good pie, Stewie.

16:41.250 --> 16:43.752
You should be proud of yourself,
whatever happens.

16:43.753 --> 16:48.340
Good afternoon, Quahog,
I'm Tom Tucker... in a T-shirt?

16:48.341 --> 16:50.383
And now, the moment
you've all been waiting for.

16:50.384 --> 16:54.095
This year's Quahog
pie-baking champion is...

16:54.096 --> 16:56.264
Fjurg Vanderploeg.

16:57.475 --> 17:00.393
Everyone is welcome to taste my pie.

17:00.394 --> 17:02.812
Sorry, Stewie. You did your best.

17:02.813 --> 17:04.606
These were old pros.

17:04.607 --> 17:06.108
But, hey, look. You took fifth.

17:07.735 --> 17:09.778
Fifth? Is that good?

17:09.779 --> 17:11.821
- Do I get a medal?
- You get a ribbon.

17:11.822 --> 17:13.990
Does everyone who participates
get a ribbon?

17:13.991 --> 17:15.742
Only ten out of 14.

17:15.743 --> 17:18.411
My God. I did it.

17:18.412 --> 17:20.497
No, Stewie, you did it...

17:20.498 --> 17:22.415
Oh, wait. Sorry, I thought you...

17:22.416 --> 17:24.709
- I thought you said "we did it."
- I did not.

17:24.710 --> 17:26.294
Good job, little boy.

17:26.295 --> 17:28.505
Maybe someday you can come by my store

17:28.506 --> 17:30.674
and have all the cake you want.

17:30.675 --> 17:33.510
- Ooh, that sounds promising.
- Okay, that's enough.

17:33.511 --> 17:36.972
And maybe this winter, you
can go fishing in my ice hole.

17:36.973 --> 17:38.640
I said enough!

17:50.736 --> 17:53.363
I think I went too big with the boots.

17:53.364 --> 17:55.907
Buddy, I think you might be
in the wrong place.

17:55.908 --> 17:59.119
Yeah, you get lost on the wrong
side of town, boot boy?

17:59.120 --> 18:00.328
- Peter.
- Just go with it.

18:00.329 --> 18:01.621
It's all part of the ruse.

18:01.622 --> 18:04.291
I say we take his pants down,
see what he's working with.

18:04.292 --> 18:06.793
And while we're at it,
give me that pool cue.

18:06.794 --> 18:08.670
I got an idea where we can put it.

18:08.671 --> 18:12.257
- Peter, shut up.
- Carter? Is that you?

18:12.258 --> 18:14.676
Oh. Hey, Babs.
I hang out here all the time.

18:14.677 --> 18:16.344
Yeah. He comes in here with me.

18:16.345 --> 18:19.139
And I'd even take
a lie detector test to prove it.

18:19.140 --> 18:23.184
Well, good thing the bar is
having Lie Detector Wednesday.

18:23.185 --> 18:24.353
Wh-What?

18:25.771 --> 18:27.689
Just a few easy warm-up questions.

18:27.690 --> 18:30.233
Have you ever had condomless sex
with a man?

18:30.234 --> 18:32.485
Okay, test over. Carter's
never been here in his life.

18:32.486 --> 18:34.822
Damn it, Peter. I'm leaving.

18:40.828 --> 18:43.997
My truck!

18:43.998 --> 18:46.625
Time to waste this fancy-pants.

18:53.716 --> 18:56.134
Babs, you saved me.

18:56.135 --> 18:58.053
And the bartender's unconscious.

18:58.054 --> 19:00.221
Let's take his pants down,
see what he's working with.

19:05.811 --> 19:08.063
Babs, I'm sorry.

19:08.064 --> 19:10.523
I tried, but I can't do it.

19:10.524 --> 19:13.526
I'll never be the real man
you want me to be.

19:13.527 --> 19:17.489
I'll always be just a spoiled,
spineless, rich dandy.

19:17.490 --> 19:20.617
Carter, I appreciate you trying
to be the man I want,

19:20.618 --> 19:24.621
but being back home here
has made me realize

19:24.622 --> 19:26.998
you already are.

19:26.999 --> 19:29.000
What? I am?

19:29.001 --> 19:32.462
I've discovered I'm not
the same girl I once was.

19:32.463 --> 19:33.963
I've changed.

19:33.964 --> 19:37.008
I've grown accustomed to life with you.

19:37.009 --> 19:39.052
I thought I wanted this life back,

19:39.053 --> 19:41.554
but have you ever had
a Milwaukee's Best?

19:41.555 --> 19:44.140
It's an awful, awful, awful...

19:44.141 --> 19:47.143
- It's one of our sponsors.
- Delicious beer,

19:47.144 --> 19:51.064
but, still, ours is the life I want,

19:51.065 --> 19:53.817
and you are the man I want.

19:53.818 --> 19:58.113
Newport is my home now,
and I'm ready to go back there.

19:58.114 --> 20:00.115
Oh, Babs.

20:01.992 --> 20:04.452
Ah, old love.

20:09.667 --> 20:13.795
Well, I didn't pay for my beer,
but I left a hell of a tip.

20:18.426 --> 20:20.301
Damn it, Griffin!
You've been staring at that menu

20:20.302 --> 20:24.181
for 22 minutes, and now you're
sitting in a double pee puddle!

20:30.187 --> 20:31.855
Peter, I'm so relieved

20:31.856 --> 20:33.773
that my mother's back with my dad.

20:33.774 --> 20:35.275
Yep. It all worked out.

20:35.276 --> 20:37.026
Only one thing left to do.

20:37.027 --> 20:40.197
Get drunk, go upstairs
and weird out the kids.

20:41.198 --> 20:43.116
Chris.

20:43.117 --> 20:46.202
Are-are you awake?

20:46.203 --> 20:50.875
Chris, you... do you want a...
You want a Tom Brady kiss?

20:51.625 --> 20:52.709
Chris, wake up.

20:52.710 --> 20:56.004
I-I want to give my son
a Tom Brady kiss.

20:56.005 --> 21:57.005
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.tv